  "features": [
    "Nine connected SQL/SQLite/FFI registry modules execute from Home-owned generation.",
    "SQLite statement binding compiles as a Home-owned standalone object; native FFI class compiles in the owned unity graph. Both headers participate in exact ABI and cache validation.",
    "Fifteen selected implementation/header files match the Bun source pin exactly.",
    "Obsolete corpus filename bypass is removed: corpus files execute through the full-VM coordinator with complete journals; explicit child VM dispatch remains intact."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The initial SQLite files exited successfully through the legacy direct-VM route but produced no journal; those attempts receive no verified corpus credit.",
    "Disk-guard stops/refusals, obsolete-cache cleanup, and the test-side environment mistake are retained without final passing credit.",
    "Ten upstream FFI skips remain separate. PostgreSQL/MySQL live-service, wider SQL/FFI behavior, remaining native/module ownership, full Bun suite and Release/ASAN/all-platform parity are not established by this checkpoint."
  ],
